{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vodi9MbQoAi5wWtD9Cji1J","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t/* Complete search over customer closing orders -- the C port.\n     2\t *\n     3\t * A faithful translation of `decide()` in customer_search.py, which is the\n     4\t * reference: where the two could differ, the Python is right and this is\n     5\t * wrong. `tests/test_native.py` checks them against each other exhaustively,\n     6\t * because a search that disagrees with its reference produces refutations that\n     7\t * are confidently false, and a refutation is the half of an optimality claim\n     8\t * nobody can check by inspection.\n     9\t *\n    10\t * Why it exists: Chu & Stuckey (2009) close 125-125-2 in about 19 minutes with\n    11\t * this algorithm in C++. The Python here does not close it at all, and the gap\n    12\t * is very largely the language.\n    13\t *\n    14\t * Customer sets are 128-bit words, which covers the whole benchmark tree (125\n    15\t * customers is the largest). Above that the caller must stay on the Python.\n    16\t */\n    17\t\n    18\t#include <stdint.h>\n    19\t#include <stdlib.h>\n    20\t#include <string.h>\n    21\t#include <time.h>\n    22\t\n    23\ttypedef unsigned __int128 mask_t;\n    24\t\n    25\t/* Fan order among equal-cost candidates. INDEX is what every run before\n    26\t * 2026-09-26 used and stays the default; DEGREE is the flag of plan 2 §2.5a. */\n    27\t#define FAN_ORDER_INDEX  0\n    28\t#define FAN_ORDER_DEGREE 1\n    29\t\n    30\t/* Variants of the 2026-09-26 `better_move` fix (0eb33915), for measuring\n    31\t * which of its two changes carries its cost (reports/ml_nature.md §31). Each\n    32\t * bit *reverts* one change; 0 is today's rule, 3 is the rule as it stood\n    33\t * before the fix under the `csearch` configuration. Both reverted forms are\n    34\t * unsound (reports/better_move_bug.md §7) and exist only to be measured. */\n    35\t#define BM_OLD_CLOSE_COUNT 1   /* count customers r finishes alone as stacks q closes */\n    36\t#define BM_OLD_RULE_ORDER  2   /* better move before the subset rule, which then cites discarded candidates */\n    37\t/* Not a revert: a candidate composition. Better move first over every\n    38\t * candidate, then the subset rule over its survivors citing only customers\n    39\t * better move did not discard, so no chain of coverings can point back at a\n    40\t * discarded candidate. Measured as `bm-first`; today's rule is unchanged. */\n    41\t#define BM_SUBSET_RESTRICTED 4\n    42\t\n    43\t#define BIT(i)        (((mask_t) 1) << (i))\n    44\t#define LOWEST(x)     ((x) & -(x))\n    45\t\n    46\tstatic inline int popcount128(mask_t x) {\n    47\t    return __builtin_popcountll((uint64_t) x) +\n    48\t           __builtin_popcountll((uint64_t) (x >> 64));\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\tstatic inline int lowest_index(mask_t x) {\n    52\t    uint64_t low = (uint64_t) x;\n    53\t    return low ? __builtin_ctzll(low) : 64 + __builtin_ctzll((uint64_t)(x >> 64));\n    54\t}\n    55\t\n    56\t/* Open-addressing set of refuted states. The Python uses a Python set with a\n    57\t * cap; this is the same idea with linear probing. Zero marks an empty slot,\n    58\t * which is safe because the empty closed-set is never refuted: it is the root,\n    59\t * and reaching it again would mean the whole search had already failed. */\n    60\ttypedef struct {\n    61\t    mask_t  *slots;\n    62\t    size_t   capacity;      /* a power of two, or 0 when memoisation is off */\n    63\t    size_t   used;\n    64\t    size_t   limit;\n    65\t} memo_t;\n    66\t\n    67\tstatic int memo_init(memo_t *m, size_t capacity, size_t limit) {\n    68\t    m->slots = calloc(capacity, sizeof(mask_t));\n    69\t    if (!m->slots) return 0;\n    70\t    m->capacity = capacity;\n    71\t    m->used = 0;\n    72\t    m->limit = limit;\n    73\t    return 1;\n    74\t}\n    75\t\n    76\tstatic inline size_t memo_hash(mask_t key, size_t capacity) {\n    77\t    uint64_t h = (uint64_t) key ^ ((uint64_t)(key >> 64) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL);\n    78\t    h ^= h >> 29; h *= 0xBF58476D1CE4E5B9ULL; h ^= h >> 32;\n    79\t    return (size_t) h & (capacity - 1);\n    80\t}\n    81\t\n    82\tstatic int memo_has(const memo_t *m, mask_t key) {\n    83\t    if (!m->capacity) return 0;\n    84\t    size_t i = memo_hash(key, m->capacity);\n    85\t    while (m->slots[i]) {\n    86\t        if (m->slots[i] == key) return 1;\n    87\t        i = (i + 1) & (m->capacity - 1);\n    88\t    }\n    89\t    return 0;\n    90\t}\n    91\t\n    92\tstatic void memo_add(memo_t *m, mask_t key) {\n    93\t    /* Stop filling past the limit, and never past 70% load: linear probing\n    94\t     * degrades badly when full, and an unbounded table on a multi-day run is\n    95\t     * how a machine dies. */\n    96\t    if (!m->capacity || m->used >= m->limit ||\n    97\t        m->used * 10 >= m->capacity * 7) return;\n    98\t    size_t i = memo_hash(key, m->capacity);\n    99\t    while (m->slots[i]) {\n   100\t        if (m->slots[i] == key) return;\n   101\t        i = (i + 1) & (m->capacity - 1);\n   102\t    }\n   103\t    m->slots[i] = key;\n   104\t    m->used++;\n   105\t}\n   106\t\n   107\ttypedef struct {\n   108\t    int      n;                 /* active customers */\n   109\t    int      k;                 /* the budget on open stacks */\n   110\t    mask_t   full;\n   111\t    mask_t  *neighbour;         /* self-inclusive neighbourhoods */\n   112\t    memo_t   memo;\n   113\t    int      subset_rule;\n   114\t    int      definite_move;\n   115\t    int      better_move;\n   116\t    int      better_move_dominators;   /* how many q to try; 0 for all */\n   117\t    int      better_move_variant;      /* BM_OLD_* bits; 0 is today's rule */\n   118\t    int      old_move;\n   119\t    int      fan_order;         /* 0: ties by customer index; 1: by remaining degree, highest